{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge","kind":"proposition","title":"Frobenius restriction: $V_{(2,1)} \\!\\downarrow_{H_2} = V_{(2)} \\oplus V_{(1,1)}$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim"],"cites":["references/wenzl1988c","references/jones1987"],"tags":["frobenius-reciprocity","branching","lepton","meson","standard-representation","entanglement","hoefsmit"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.standard_restricts_to_both_leptons","text":"frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.md","leanSource":"frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge\"></a><p>The standard representation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_{(2,1)}</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(q)</code> restricts to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_2(q)</code> as the direct sum of its two one-dimensional irreducible representations:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  V_{(2,1)} \\big\\downarrow_{H_2}\n  = V_{(2)} \\oplus V_{(1,1)}.</code></pre>\n<p>At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_2</code>, the irreps <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_{(2)}</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_{(1,1)}</code> are separate. At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3</code>, they are coupled inside the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2 \\times 2</code> Hoefsmit block of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_{(2,1)}</code>. The off-diagonal element</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  b = \\sqrt{a_\\rho \\cdot a_{-\\rho} + 1},\n  \\qquad\n  a_\\rho = \\frac{h}{1 - q^{-2\\rho}},</code></pre>\n<p>couples the two channels; they decouple exactly when <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b = 0</code>.</p>\n<p>By Frobenius reciprocity:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\langle \\mathrm{Res}(V_{(2,1)}), V_{(2)} \\rangle_{H_2}\n  = \\langle V_{(2,1)}, \\mathrm{Ind}(V_{(2)}) \\rangle_{H_3}\n  = 1.</code></pre>\n<p>Each one-dimensional irreducible representation of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_2(q)</code> appears exactly once in the restriction.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"7.10.1","page":"b/prop-frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge","qa":{"counts":{"pass":97,"fail":1,"warn":2,"na":15,"unknown":0,"stale":89},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.standard_restricts_to_both_leptons","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
